1
00:00:01,125 --> 00:00:02,835
- "Previously on The Mentalist..."
- Grace and I

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:05,463
we always thought that you
and Lisbon would get together.

3
00:00:10,468 --> 00:00:12,345
"This is
Special Agent Marcus Pike."

4
00:00:12,470 --> 00:00:14,514
"He's being attached to our team
while we work the case."

5
00:00:14,639 --> 00:00:16,933
I like you and I think you're
a hell of a good-looking woman

6
00:00:17,058 --> 00:00:18,392
and I'd love
to get to know you better.

7
00:00:18,851 --> 00:00:21,521
If the offer still stands
the answer is yes.

8
00:00:22,188 --> 00:00:23,231
Let's get married.

9
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:24,982
Yes.

10
00:00:27,151 --> 00:00:28,194
Wait!

11
00:00:29,737 --> 00:00:30,780
What are you doing here?

12
00:00:30,905 --> 00:00:31,989
There's something
I need to say.

13
00:00:32,865 --> 00:00:35,243
The truth is I love you.

14
00:00:35,952 --> 00:00:37,411
Did you mean what you said?

15
00:00:37,954 --> 00:00:39,997
- Yes, I did.
- Good.

16
00:01:23,833 --> 00:01:24,875
Hello?

17
00:01:35,428 --> 00:01:36,470
I know you.

18
00:01:39,348 --> 00:01:40,391
I know you.

19
00:01:54,196 --> 00:01:55,865
- Morning.
- Morning.

20
00:02:13,257 --> 00:02:14,300
Hey.

21
00:02:14,425 --> 00:02:15,760
- Your coffee.
- Thank you.

22
00:02:16,510 --> 00:02:17,970
It's a beautiful day.
You wanna sit out here?

23
00:02:18,137 --> 00:02:19,639
Yeah, you can just push
all that stuff to the side.

24
00:02:19,764 --> 00:02:20,848
It's going in the garage.

25
00:02:22,850 --> 00:02:25,144
I'll take it around there
in a minute.

26
00:02:26,812 --> 00:02:28,481
- It's a lovely day.
- Yeah.

27
00:02:33,819 --> 00:02:36,030
Should think about getting you
a key to this place, huh?

28
00:02:38,783 --> 00:02:39,867
Well, that's a step.

29
00:02:40,284 --> 00:02:42,370
- Yeah.
- Uh, it would make things easier.

30
00:02:46,123 --> 00:02:47,166
Okay.

31
00:02:47,875 --> 00:02:50,002
What do we have in here? Hm?

32
00:02:51,504 --> 00:02:54,590
Vintage car? Well, that should definitely
be garaged.

33
00:02:55,883 --> 00:02:58,010
You don't really strike me
as a vintage-car kinda girl.

34
00:02:58,219 --> 00:03:01,138
It was a graduation gift
from my grandfather.

35
00:03:01,847 --> 00:03:03,140
I think it was his favorite.

36
00:03:05,351 --> 00:03:07,228
Thank you for helping
move all this.

37
00:03:10,898 --> 00:03:12,108
It's my pleasure.

38
00:03:14,068 --> 00:03:15,403
It's been nice.

39
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:21,242
We're gonna have to get back into
the real world at some point, though.

40
00:03:22,326 --> 00:03:26,163
- Yeah. Really?
- Really.

41
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:31,752
Do you wanna talk about
how we're gonna do that, maybe, or...

42
00:03:33,713 --> 00:03:34,755
Sure.

43
00:03:36,132 --> 00:03:37,174
Okay.

44
00:03:39,677 --> 00:03:40,720
Sorry.

45
00:03:43,514 --> 00:03:44,557
Abbott.

46
00:03:45,891 --> 00:03:47,685
- What's up, boss?
- "Lisbon!"

47
00:03:47,935 --> 00:03:50,020
"I know you still have time left
on your leave"

48
00:03:50,813 --> 00:03:52,690
"but I need your help.
Do you mind suiting up?"

49
00:03:53,065 --> 00:03:54,400
Not at all.
What's the case?

50
00:03:54,525 --> 00:03:56,026
It's a homicide.
It's complicated.

51
00:03:56,152 --> 00:03:57,445
- I'll text you the address.
- "Okay."

52
00:03:57,611 --> 00:03:58,779
You know where I can find Jane?

53
00:03:59,155 --> 00:04:00,698
I have no idea where he is.

54
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:02,783
All right.
I'll track him down.

55
00:04:03,117 --> 00:04:04,326
- Okay.
- "See you there."

56
00:04:04,702 --> 00:04:05,745
Bye.

57
00:04:07,955 --> 00:04:09,915
You really have no idea
where I am?

58
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:12,460
It just seemed like
the thing to say.

59
00:04:13,753 --> 00:04:15,755
- You embarrassed?
- No! God, no.

60
00:04:15,963 --> 00:04:17,298
It's okay
if you're embarrassed.

61
00:04:17,423 --> 00:04:21,552
No, it's just... things with Marcus
just sort of went down

62
00:04:21,677 --> 00:04:25,431
and I just would like
to keep my private life private.

63
00:04:25,639 --> 00:04:28,851
Just for the moment.
Not forever or anything, and...

64
00:04:30,936 --> 00:04:32,813
- Is that okay?
- Yeah, sure. That's fine.

65
00:04:33,314 --> 00:04:34,940
- Don't worry. Yeah.
- You're sure?

66
00:04:35,274 --> 00:04:36,525
- Okay.
- I understand.

67
00:04:36,859 --> 00:04:37,902
Okay.

68
00:04:40,696 --> 00:04:42,239
- My turn.
- Okay.

69
00:04:44,074 --> 00:04:45,117
Hi, Abbott.

70
00:04:51,832 --> 00:04:53,626
Hey, Cho.
How you doing?

71
00:04:54,001 --> 00:04:55,795
- Good. You?
- I'm good.

72
00:04:57,296 --> 00:04:59,089
- Not going to Washington?
- No.

73
00:04:59,215 --> 00:05:00,883
- Not marrying Pike?
- No.

74
00:05:01,759 --> 00:05:02,802
Okay.

75
00:05:03,177 --> 00:05:05,471
Victim's name
is Jeremy Geist. Shot twice.

76
00:05:05,930 --> 00:05:08,349
Some customers from the bowling alley
found him a little after 2 A.M.

77
00:05:08,516 --> 00:05:09,642
Apparently, he was a regular.

78
00:05:09,767 --> 00:05:11,018
Looks like
a run-of-the-mill homicide.

79
00:05:11,143 --> 00:05:13,062
Can't Austin P.D. handle it?
What are we doing here?

80
00:05:13,187 --> 00:05:14,730
You got me.
Abbott just said "get here".

81
00:05:15,147 --> 00:05:18,317
Hey, Cho.
Gimme some sugar, baby.

82
00:05:19,193 --> 00:05:20,236
There we are.

83
00:05:22,488 --> 00:05:23,531
- Looking good.
- Thanks.

84
00:05:23,781 --> 00:05:25,241
- Hey, Lisbon.
- Jane.

85
00:05:25,741 --> 00:05:26,784
Look good, too.

86
00:05:27,409 --> 00:05:28,744
Got some pecan nuts.
You want some?

87
00:05:29,078 --> 00:05:30,120
Um, no.

88
00:05:30,746 --> 00:05:31,789
I could...

89
00:05:32,957 --> 00:05:34,166
- You?
- No, thanks.

90
00:05:34,834 --> 00:05:36,252
Okay. More for me.

91
00:05:37,211 --> 00:05:38,546
- Boss.
- Hey.

92
00:05:38,879 --> 00:05:39,922
Hey, Abbott.

93
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:42,550
Well, we have to be careful
with this one.

94
00:05:42,842 --> 00:05:44,760
Austin P.D. doesn't know it,
but...

95
00:05:45,469 --> 00:05:48,013
the victim, Geist,
was FBI working undercover.

96
00:05:49,557 --> 00:05:51,141
And we are not releasing that.

97
00:05:52,226 --> 00:05:54,353
So, gather whatever information
you can.

98
00:05:54,770 --> 00:05:56,814
Get back to the office.
We're being briefed in an hour.

99
00:05:57,398 --> 00:05:59,400
Cho, let's go talk
to the lead officer in charge.

100
00:05:59,608 --> 00:06:00,651
Yep.

101
00:06:03,737 --> 00:06:05,698
- That went okay, huh?
- Yeah, I thought it went very well.

102
00:06:05,823 --> 00:06:08,576
I'm gonna head back to the office.
Uh, see you later.

103
00:06:09,034 --> 00:06:11,203
- What is that in your pocket?
- What?

104
00:06:40,439 --> 00:06:42,900
All right. Can I have
everyone's attention please.

105
00:06:44,109 --> 00:06:45,444
This is Ken Spackman.

106
00:06:46,445 --> 00:06:49,907
He's running the joint
FBI and ATF task force

107
00:06:50,282 --> 00:06:52,034
that sent
Jeremy Geist undercover.

108
00:06:53,076 --> 00:06:54,995
I just notified his family
in Pittsburgh.

109
00:06:55,412 --> 00:06:57,539
{\an8}This is uh...
This is such a blow.

110
00:06:57,915 --> 00:07:00,542
{\an8}Jeremy was
a first-rate agent. So...

111
00:07:00,751 --> 00:07:03,045
{\an8}Big blow for them, I'm sure.
Not so much for you, though.

112
00:07:03,253 --> 00:07:05,923
{\an8}- You barely knew Geist.
- That's correct.

113
00:07:06,048 --> 00:07:08,008
{\an8}Um, he came to us
from the Savannah office

114
00:07:08,133 --> 00:07:09,217
{\an8}a few months back.

115
00:07:10,010 --> 00:07:12,095
{\an8}We needed somebody who wouldn't
be recognized in Austin.

116
00:07:12,638 --> 00:07:13,847
{\an8}Uh, what was the assignment?

117
00:07:14,598 --> 00:07:17,142
{\an8}There's a gang that's been stealing
military-issue firearms

118
00:07:17,267 --> 00:07:19,478
{\an8}from army bases and selling them
to drug dealers.

119
00:07:19,770 --> 00:07:23,231
{\an8}So, we got a report
that the Rocket Bowl parking lot

120
00:07:23,357 --> 00:07:25,400
{\an8}is where the guns were
changing hands.

121
00:07:25,525 --> 00:07:27,945
{\an8}We figured somebody there was
involved, likely as a salesman.

122
00:07:28,236 --> 00:07:31,698
{\an8}We sent Geist in undercover
in hopes that he could tell us who it was.

123
00:07:32,032 --> 00:07:33,075
Any luck?

124
00:07:33,283 --> 00:07:34,743
Not yet,
but he was getting close.

125
00:07:35,327 --> 00:07:37,371
{\an8}We're gonna send another agent in
in a couple weeks.

126
00:07:37,537 --> 00:07:41,875
{\an8}In the meantime, you can't
disclose that Geist was FBI.

127
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,877
{\an8}- It'll blow the whole thing.
- That's not gonna be easy.

128
00:07:44,544 --> 00:07:45,671
{\an8}There's a good chance
Geist was killed

129
00:07:45,796 --> 00:07:46,838
{\an8}because somebody
blew his cover.

130
00:07:46,964 --> 00:07:48,674
{\an8}We need to be able
to ask questions about that.

131
00:07:49,216 --> 00:07:51,385
{\an8}You have to understand
what's at stake, okay?

132
00:07:52,219 --> 00:07:53,804
{\an8}Now, we get the salesman,
we can flip him

133
00:07:53,929 --> 00:07:55,263
{\an8}which means
we can get the whole gang.

134
00:07:55,389 --> 00:07:58,016
{\an8}But if it gets out that we had
an undercover agent in place

135
00:07:58,141 --> 00:08:01,019
{\an8}then the operation will shut down
and the whole gang will scatter.

136
00:08:01,603 --> 00:08:03,522
{\an8}Well, that's not so bad.
And from the way he's acting

137
00:08:03,647 --> 00:08:05,983
{\an8}uh, there's a chance that
Spackman here is the killer.

138
00:08:06,441 --> 00:08:07,818
He's practically in our laps.

139
00:08:07,943 --> 00:08:10,529
- I'm sorry. What did you say?
- Or not. Could go either way.

140
00:08:10,862 --> 00:08:13,198
Point being, it's all fine.

141
00:08:13,824 --> 00:08:14,908
- I...
- I'm sorry, who...?

142
00:08:15,033 --> 00:08:16,785
{\an8}I think we all understand
how to do the job here.

143
00:08:16,910 --> 00:08:18,704
{\an8}So let's get ready
to roll out in 15 minutes.

144
00:08:19,037 --> 00:08:20,080
Let's.

145
00:08:32,092 --> 00:08:33,135
{\an8}Hey.

146
00:08:33,510 --> 00:08:35,762
{\an8}- Hi. Welcome back. We missed you.
- Thanks.

147
00:08:36,221 --> 00:08:37,806
Uh, where's Fischer?
Is she out sick?

148
00:08:38,140 --> 00:08:40,434
- No, she transferred.
- Really? Where?

149
00:08:40,642 --> 00:08:41,977
Seattle. Her mother's there.

150
00:08:42,102 --> 00:08:43,854
She had a stroke,
so she went to take care of her.

151
00:08:44,438 --> 00:08:47,107
{\an8}Ooh. She asked me
to give you this.

152
00:08:49,276 --> 00:08:50,652
{\an8}Abbott says they're assigning us
a rookie

153
00:08:50,777 --> 00:08:52,070
from Quantico
to fill out the team.

154
00:08:52,237 --> 00:08:53,613
That should be interesting.

155
00:08:57,284 --> 00:08:58,660
Oh, that's sweet.

156
00:08:59,244 --> 00:09:00,328
{\an8}Thank you.

157
00:09:18,180 --> 00:09:20,098
You're FBI, right?
Who's Cho?

158
00:09:20,432 --> 00:09:22,017
- I am.
- Hey, Mason Hunston.

159
00:09:22,184 --> 00:09:24,394
I'm the owner.
Anything we can do to help.

160
00:09:25,145 --> 00:09:26,605
I mean, we've had some fights
from time to time

161
00:09:26,730 --> 00:09:27,898
but nothing like this.

162
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:29,483
Were you here
when it happened?

163
00:09:29,608 --> 00:09:30,942
Uh, I was up in my office.

164
00:09:31,401 --> 00:09:33,153
Didn't know anything
until the police arrived.

165
00:09:33,695 --> 00:09:35,739
It's birthdays and bowling leagues
until about 9 p.m.

166
00:09:35,864 --> 00:09:37,365
then the drinkers take over.

167
00:09:37,824 --> 00:09:40,869
It's a rougher crowd, but we haven't had
any serious problems until now.

168
00:09:41,161 --> 00:09:42,329
Who was working last night?

169
00:09:42,662 --> 00:09:44,915
Tish and Skye. They work the bar.
They're there now.

170
00:09:45,332 --> 00:09:47,834
Uh, Wick Ammon. He's our bouncer.
He's over there.

171
00:09:47,959 --> 00:09:49,961
And, uh, Andy the shoe guy.

172
00:09:51,171 --> 00:09:52,881
- Anything else?
- Yeah, I have a question.

173
00:09:53,131 --> 00:09:56,593
Uh, what's the best way to turn
a 10-7 split into a spare?

174
00:09:57,594 --> 00:09:58,720
Um...

175
00:09:59,805 --> 00:10:01,264
Line up on the 7 pin.

176
00:10:02,516 --> 00:10:05,018
Aim for the far side,
hit it hard as you can.

177
00:10:05,143 --> 00:10:09,773
Just try to get that pin action.
I got it.

178
00:10:10,565 --> 00:10:12,567
- Anything else?
- No. Thanks for your help.

179
00:10:16,571 --> 00:10:17,614
Mr. Ammon?

180
00:10:20,117 --> 00:10:21,159
- Wick Ammon?
- Yes.

181
00:10:21,326 --> 00:10:22,744
Agent Kimball Cho, FBI.

182
00:10:22,869 --> 00:10:24,538
I understand you were working
security here last night.

183
00:10:24,704 --> 00:10:26,081
You mind answering
a few questions?

184
00:10:26,498 --> 00:10:28,041
Agent Kimball Cho of the FBI

185
00:10:28,166 --> 00:10:30,710
know that I am a sovereign
citizen of the state of Texas

186
00:10:30,836 --> 00:10:33,421
and do not recognize the legitimacy
of the federal government

187
00:10:33,547 --> 00:10:36,174
or any police authority
you may claim to possess.

188
00:10:37,300 --> 00:10:39,594
Nonetheless, I will answer
your questions voluntarily.

189
00:10:39,803 --> 00:10:41,429
Great. Did you see Jeremy Geist
here last night?

190
00:10:41,638 --> 00:10:43,473
I did. He arrived a little after 11.

191
00:10:43,598 --> 00:10:45,684
Didn't see him leave, though.
Must've gone out through the side door.

192
00:10:45,892 --> 00:10:48,186
- Did you talk to him?
- Said hello when he arrived.

193
00:10:48,395 --> 00:10:49,437
Let me ask you something, agent.

194
00:10:49,855 --> 00:10:52,482
Are you aware that the government
you've sworn allegiance to

195
00:10:52,607 --> 00:10:54,901
is illegitimate
and illegally constituted?

196
00:10:55,026 --> 00:10:56,695
Yes. Did you notice
anything about him?

197
00:10:57,195 --> 00:10:59,573
Just that he kept to himself,
didn't talk much to people.

198
00:11:00,365 --> 00:11:02,450
You also know
that federal income tax

199
00:11:02,576 --> 00:11:04,119
is government-sanctioned theft

200
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:06,955
intended to prop up
a global conspiracy of bankers?

201
00:11:08,790 --> 00:11:11,751
Tish. Did you notice Jeremy
arguing with anybody last night?

202
00:11:12,586 --> 00:11:13,628
Nope.

203
00:11:14,629 --> 00:11:15,922
Hardly spoke to anyone.

204
00:11:16,631 --> 00:11:19,426
Pretty friendly most days,
but he didn't say five words.

205
00:11:19,968 --> 00:11:21,261
So he wasn't drinking then.

206
00:11:22,470 --> 00:11:24,848
- Club soda.
- Oh, well.

207
00:11:24,973 --> 00:11:28,310
I would guess that's unusual
for a three-beer-a-night kinda guy.

208
00:11:30,353 --> 00:11:32,397
Yeah. It is.

209
00:11:33,523 --> 00:11:36,318
What about you, Skye? Did you notice
anything odd about Jeremy last night?

210
00:11:36,568 --> 00:11:38,028
Not last night so much.

211
00:11:38,195 --> 00:11:39,905
There was something strange
two nights ago.

212
00:11:40,113 --> 00:11:41,156
What?

213
00:11:41,406 --> 00:11:43,033
Jeremy was fine
when he got here.

214
00:11:43,658 --> 00:11:46,328
A little while later,
he just shut down.

215
00:11:46,912 --> 00:11:49,831
He sat at the bar,
he wouldn't talk to anybody.

216
00:11:50,290 --> 00:11:52,709
Did he seem angry,
scared, sad?

217
00:11:53,335 --> 00:11:56,171
Spooked. He looked really spooked.

218
00:11:58,089 --> 00:12:00,300
Yeah, I go to the bar sometime.
When my shift is over.

219
00:12:01,468 --> 00:12:02,510
Just to hang.

220
00:12:02,719 --> 00:12:03,845
- Just to hang?
- Yeah.

221
00:12:04,095 --> 00:12:06,223
Did you ever, uh? Did you ever
talk to Jeremy Geist

222
00:12:06,348 --> 00:12:07,390
when you went over there, Andy?

223
00:12:08,099 --> 00:12:09,976
Yeah. Sure.
Jeremy's a good guy.

224
00:12:11,519 --> 00:12:14,147
- What'd you two talk about?
- I don't know.

225
00:12:14,606 --> 00:12:17,067
- Sports, I guess. Um...
- Sports, you guess?

226
00:12:17,275 --> 00:12:19,611
Bikes. You know, like that.

227
00:12:20,528 --> 00:12:23,615
So, what does this have to do
with him getting murdered?

228
00:12:26,952 --> 00:12:28,078
Are you nervous, Andy?

229
00:12:29,204 --> 00:12:30,247
- No. Yeah.
- You sure?

230
00:12:30,372 --> 00:12:32,374
- You seem kinda nervous. Okay.
- No. Not at all.

231
00:12:33,250 --> 00:12:34,292
"Hey, Spackman!"

232
00:12:37,462 --> 00:12:39,256
- Will you excuse me?
- Sure.

233
00:12:43,134 --> 00:12:44,970
- This isn't working.
- Uh, I don't agree.

234
00:12:45,387 --> 00:12:47,347
Our boy Andy over there,
he's wound up about something.

235
00:12:47,472 --> 00:12:48,515
I think he's about to crack.

236
00:12:48,765 --> 00:12:51,351
Uh, he's carrying drugs.

237
00:12:51,768 --> 00:12:53,687
But if you want to bust someone
that has painkillers

238
00:12:53,812 --> 00:12:56,648
without a prescription
he's definitely your man.

239
00:12:57,482 --> 00:12:59,109
- You're calling that from here?
- Yes.

240
00:12:59,526 --> 00:13:00,860
It is difficult to get anything

241
00:13:00,986 --> 00:13:03,113
if we can't talk about
why Geist was here.

242
00:13:03,405 --> 00:13:05,282
- Listen, I can't help you there.
- You're gonna have to.

243
00:13:05,657 --> 00:13:07,784
I understand you wanna protect
your investigation

244
00:13:07,909 --> 00:13:08,952
but this is a waste of time.

245
00:13:09,077 --> 00:13:11,454
I thought you guys
were some innovative team

246
00:13:11,579 --> 00:13:13,623
that was capable
of working outside the box

247
00:13:13,748 --> 00:13:15,500
so what is
with your whining?

248
00:13:15,792 --> 00:13:17,836
- Don't talk to her like that.
- We are not whining.

249
00:13:17,961 --> 00:13:19,004
Yeah, it sounds like
you're whining.

250
00:13:19,129 --> 00:13:20,171
You don't have
to talk to her like that...

251
00:13:20,297 --> 00:13:22,340
- Hey. Back off.
- I won't back off.

252
00:13:22,465 --> 00:13:24,092
You needn't talk to her
like that.

253
00:13:25,844 --> 00:13:27,887
Look, we've spent
a lot of time and energy

254
00:13:28,013 --> 00:13:30,223
trying to figure out who is
selling guns in this place.

255
00:13:30,432 --> 00:13:31,850
And we're not gonna
let you guys come in

256
00:13:32,100 --> 00:13:33,351
and mess up our investigation

257
00:13:33,476 --> 00:13:35,812
until that person has been
identified and arrested.

258
00:13:35,937 --> 00:13:37,772
- Do you got me?
- Fine.

259
00:13:38,565 --> 00:13:39,607
Where is he going?

260
00:13:39,983 --> 00:13:41,484
Can I have your attention please?

261
00:13:42,485 --> 00:13:45,488
Thank you. There are these
things called microexpressions.

262
00:13:45,739 --> 00:13:48,033
They are what shows on your face
when you feel something.

263
00:13:48,158 --> 00:13:49,826
They're automatic.
You can't control them.

264
00:13:49,993 --> 00:13:52,579
So when I tell you that Jeremy Geist

265
00:13:52,704 --> 00:13:55,040
was an FBI agent
working undercover

266
00:13:55,332 --> 00:13:57,417
everyone... Yes, there they are.

267
00:13:57,959 --> 00:13:59,794
Showed a brief expression
of surprise.

268
00:13:59,919 --> 00:14:02,005
- What the hell?
- His was bigger than most.

269
00:14:02,172 --> 00:14:04,799
But when I tell you that Jeremy Geist
was investigating a gang

270
00:14:04,924 --> 00:14:06,926
selling illegal firearms
out of this bar

271
00:14:07,052 --> 00:14:09,346
only one person will show fear.

272
00:14:09,512 --> 00:14:12,932
The person
who is afraid of being caught.

273
00:14:13,141 --> 00:14:15,518
And that person is...

274
00:14:18,521 --> 00:14:19,773
It's you, Tish.

275
00:14:21,274 --> 00:14:23,401
- What?
- It's literally on your face.

276
00:14:23,526 --> 00:14:24,986
There is your salesman.

277
00:14:45,048 --> 00:14:46,299
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

278
00:14:50,136 --> 00:14:51,930
Wow. She was fast.

279
00:15:07,543 --> 00:15:08,585
"Can I help you?"

280
00:15:09,294 --> 00:15:11,213
I'm looking for
Supervisory Agent Abbott.

281
00:15:11,547 --> 00:15:13,382
Yeah, oh, uh,
down that way, second door.

282
00:15:14,133 --> 00:15:15,175
Thanks.

283
00:15:22,224 --> 00:15:24,226
You asked for the salesman.
I found the salesman.

284
00:15:24,351 --> 00:15:26,228
- Sales... The, the woman Saleswoman.
- Yeah.

285
00:15:26,395 --> 00:15:27,479
Only we don't have her now.

286
00:15:28,022 --> 00:15:30,232
See, she's in the wind.
She's probably across the border already.

287
00:15:30,357 --> 00:15:33,527
Oh, now, she needs to get ready
before she leaves the country.

288
00:15:33,986 --> 00:15:36,113
She'll need a little time.
We'll find her, Ken.

289
00:15:36,238 --> 00:15:37,698
See? Every... Everything's fine.

290
00:15:38,282 --> 00:15:40,117
No. No.
It is not fine.

291
00:15:40,367 --> 00:15:42,286
First of all,
you haven't got any evidence.

292
00:15:42,661 --> 00:15:44,913
And, you know, even if we do
manage to bring her in

293
00:15:45,497 --> 00:15:47,499
what am I gonna do?
Pressure her with your say so?

294
00:15:47,833 --> 00:15:49,501
I can't exactly get her to give up
the names

295
00:15:49,626 --> 00:15:51,336
of the people
that she's working with, why?

296
00:15:51,462 --> 00:15:52,755
Just because you say she did it?

297
00:15:53,422 --> 00:15:55,591
All I can do now
is hold her for two days

298
00:15:56,008 --> 00:15:57,968
while her lawyer sits there
and laughs at me

299
00:15:58,093 --> 00:15:59,595
and while the rest
of her crew disperses.

300
00:15:59,720 --> 00:16:02,139
So this is not okay.
This is a disaster.

301
00:16:02,598 --> 00:16:04,099
He's not wrong.

302
00:16:05,476 --> 00:16:09,313
Well, it's, it's possible
that I was a tad hasty.

303
00:16:09,688 --> 00:16:11,023
But you got my ire up.

304
00:16:11,148 --> 00:16:12,274
- Uh...
- Can I help you?

305
00:16:12,816 --> 00:16:15,319
Michelle Vega. I was told to report
for assignment to your unit.

306
00:16:15,694 --> 00:16:16,945
Vega. Right.

307
00:16:17,154 --> 00:16:18,530
Agent Vega, Patrick Jane.

308
00:16:18,781 --> 00:16:19,823
- Welcome.
- Thank you.

309
00:16:19,990 --> 00:16:21,867
- Pleased to be here, sir.
- Oh, you don't have to call me sir.

310
00:16:21,992 --> 00:16:23,660
In fact,
please don't call me sir.

311
00:16:23,994 --> 00:16:25,037
Save it for him.

312
00:16:25,704 --> 00:16:27,498
Congratulations.
First assignment, huh?

313
00:16:27,956 --> 00:16:31,043
I also see that you're, uh,
former military.

314
00:16:31,877 --> 00:16:33,545
Uh, no.

315
00:16:34,755 --> 00:16:38,342
Interesting that you would lie to me
so early in our acquaintance.

316
00:16:39,384 --> 00:16:42,679
Uh, I, I wouldn't.
I mean, I'm not.

317
00:16:43,472 --> 00:16:45,682
My dad was army.
Career, 37 years.

318
00:16:45,933 --> 00:16:48,143
- Dennis?
- Vega.

319
00:16:48,560 --> 00:16:49,853
Uh, could you go out
into the bullpen

320
00:16:49,978 --> 00:16:51,939
and, uh, look for Cho or Lisbon.

321
00:16:52,189 --> 00:16:54,441
They'll show you around
and I'll be out in a few minutes, okay?

322
00:16:54,775 --> 00:16:55,818
Yes, sir.

323
00:16:58,320 --> 00:17:00,405
So, gentlemen.

324
00:17:02,116 --> 00:17:03,617
- What are we doing?
- Spackman.

325
00:17:04,952 --> 00:17:06,245
I'm gonna make this up to you.

326
00:17:07,538 --> 00:17:10,499
When this is over,
it's gonna be your birthday.

327
00:17:12,334 --> 00:17:15,295
- Really.
- Candles on the cake and all, Ken.

328
00:17:18,882 --> 00:17:20,592
And this is Agent Cho.

329
00:17:21,135 --> 00:17:22,845
- Hi. Welcome.
- It's a pleasure.

330
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:24,930
- Teresa Lisbon.
- Hi.

331
00:17:25,889 --> 00:17:28,016
And then there's Abbott.
And Jane, of course.

332
00:17:28,475 --> 00:17:30,561
Jane. Is that the guy
in Abbott's office

333
00:17:30,686 --> 00:17:33,397
with the, uh... shirt?
Is he an agent?

334
00:17:33,772 --> 00:17:35,399
No, but he's part of the team.

335
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:38,068
He's, uh different.

336
00:17:38,277 --> 00:17:39,444
Anything I should know
about him?

337
00:17:39,820 --> 00:17:40,946
There's probably a few things.

338
00:17:41,321 --> 00:17:43,323
Cho, Wylie,
you're working with Spackman

339
00:17:43,448 --> 00:17:44,658
on tracking down Tish.

340
00:17:45,284 --> 00:17:47,536
- You think she killed Geist?
- Probably not. if she did

341
00:17:47,661 --> 00:17:49,496
she wouldn't have been
surprised he was FBI.

342
00:17:49,913 --> 00:17:53,167
Which means we're still looking for
a viable suspect for the murder.

343
00:17:53,584 --> 00:17:56,461
I'll call Austin P.D. to see if they can
track down the customers in the bar.

344
00:17:56,753 --> 00:17:59,089
I'm running background checks
on everybody who works in the bowling alley.

345
00:17:59,298 --> 00:18:00,340
Let's go.

346
00:18:01,425 --> 00:18:02,593
Anything I can do, sir?

347
00:18:04,011 --> 00:18:07,347
Ah, yeah. Relax, we'll talk,
and then I'll put you to work.

348
00:18:08,724 --> 00:18:09,766
Yes, sir.

349
00:18:11,101 --> 00:18:13,395
- Oh. Where you headed?
- Over to Geist's apartment.

350
00:18:13,520 --> 00:18:15,397
- Poke my nose around.
- Yeah.

351
00:18:15,522 --> 00:18:17,816
Both the bartender and the waitress
said that he was acting weird.

352
00:18:17,941 --> 00:18:19,026
Any idea
what that was about?

353
00:18:19,359 --> 00:18:21,612
- Not at all.
- Oh, great.

354
00:18:22,905 --> 00:18:24,156
You know,
I don't know what's going on

355
00:18:24,281 --> 00:18:26,992
- between you and Lisbon, but, uh...
- Nothing's going on.

356
00:18:28,702 --> 00:18:30,120
Right. Right.
I understand.

357
00:18:30,245 --> 00:18:32,164
That's the party line, right?
That's fine.

358
00:18:32,497 --> 00:18:33,540
It's all good.

359
00:18:34,082 --> 00:18:36,293
But on the off chance
that something is going on

360
00:18:36,460 --> 00:18:39,213
I thought you might wanna know
that Marcus Pike is in the building

361
00:18:39,546 --> 00:18:41,048
meeting with
a federal prosecutor.

362
00:18:41,924 --> 00:18:43,008
Just an FYI.

363
00:18:55,520 --> 00:18:57,147
"Okay, 324."

364
00:18:58,315 --> 00:19:00,984
Geist. Geist. 322. Here.

365
00:19:02,110 --> 00:19:03,195
Let me know
when you're out.

366
00:19:03,946 --> 00:19:05,155
I will, thank you.

367
00:20:26,111 --> 00:20:28,280
- Vega.
- Agent Vega. Patrick Jane.

368
00:20:28,530 --> 00:20:29,614
How're you doing?
Settling in?

369
00:20:29,823 --> 00:20:30,949
Yes, thank you.

370
00:20:31,825 --> 00:20:33,201
Is there something
I can do for you, agent?

371
00:20:33,744 --> 00:20:36,413
Yeah, you can stop calling me
agent for starters.

372
00:20:36,538 --> 00:20:39,458
Now, your father was army
but you weren't?

373
00:20:40,125 --> 00:20:42,627
- Yes, sir.
- I don't believe you.

374
00:20:43,045 --> 00:20:44,880
You have military
in your posture, Vega.

375
00:20:45,255 --> 00:20:47,466
- That is not genetic.
- Um...

376
00:20:48,759 --> 00:20:51,595
Yes, I was at the Point.
West Point.

377
00:20:52,012 --> 00:20:55,015
- But I didn't graduate.
- Oh, I'm so sorry.

378
00:20:56,099 --> 00:20:57,267
It wasn't that big a thing.

379
00:20:57,893 --> 00:21:00,270
No, not about the point.
Your, your father.

380
00:21:00,437 --> 00:21:03,815
I, uh, I'm sure that was
a very difficult time for you.

381
00:21:06,193 --> 00:21:07,402
How'd you know about that?

382
00:21:08,070 --> 00:21:09,821
Well, you don't strike me
as the type of person

383
00:21:09,946 --> 00:21:11,323
that would give up on things and...

384
00:21:11,740 --> 00:21:14,910
What else would keep you
from finishing at the Point?

385
00:21:16,953 --> 00:21:18,288
He had liver cancer.

386
00:21:19,790 --> 00:21:21,124
It was very fast.

387
00:21:22,709 --> 00:21:23,752
After that, um...

388
00:21:26,004 --> 00:21:27,881
Just wasn't that interested
in the military anymore.

389
00:21:28,173 --> 00:21:29,216
Of course not.

390
00:21:30,675 --> 00:21:31,885
Is there something
I can do for you?

391
00:21:32,677 --> 00:21:33,720
Uh, yes, there is.

392
00:21:33,845 --> 00:21:35,305
Uh, when you were at Quantico

393
00:21:35,430 --> 00:21:37,391
did they do
some sort of psychological

394
00:21:37,516 --> 00:21:41,520
or, uh, emotional-profile
test thing?

395
00:21:42,145 --> 00:21:44,398
- Yes, a pretty extensive one.
- Excellent.

396
00:21:44,523 --> 00:21:47,192
I, I need Jeremy Geist's
psychological profile.

397
00:21:47,317 --> 00:21:48,693
Do you think
you could get that for me?

398
00:21:49,694 --> 00:21:52,614
Yes. Yes, of course.
I will get right on it.

399
00:21:52,948 --> 00:21:55,409
Excellent work, Agent Vega.
As you were.

400
00:22:00,330 --> 00:22:01,373
- Hey, Cho.
- "Yes?"

401
00:22:01,665 --> 00:22:02,749
Austin P.D. just called.

402
00:22:02,874 --> 00:22:04,209
A license-plate sweep
found a truck

403
00:22:04,334 --> 00:22:06,169
registered to Tish Delaurio
in a parking garage

404
00:22:06,294 --> 00:22:08,046
- in Travis Heights.
- Anybody sitting on it?

405
00:22:08,171 --> 00:22:09,673
Two uniforms,
but it's all they can spare.

406
00:22:10,006 --> 00:22:11,758
All right. I'll get a team
out there to pick her up.

407
00:22:14,970 --> 00:22:17,180
Sir? I heard you say
you were gonna pick somebody up.

408
00:22:17,389 --> 00:22:19,474
Would it be all right if I came along?
Just to observe.

409
00:22:20,308 --> 00:22:21,560
You don't have
something else to do?

410
00:22:22,227 --> 00:22:25,480
No. Agent... I mean,
Mr. Jane asked for something

411
00:22:25,605 --> 00:22:27,649
- but it's on its way.
- Sure. You can come.

412
00:22:28,316 --> 00:22:29,359
Thanks.

413
00:22:31,695 --> 00:22:33,697
Wylie told me you worked
with Agent Lisbon in California

414
00:22:33,822 --> 00:22:34,948
before you came here.

415
00:22:36,616 --> 00:22:38,827
- Jane was there, too?
- Yeah.

416
00:22:42,122 --> 00:22:43,748
Wylie told me
he was a psychic.

417
00:22:45,292 --> 00:22:46,376
No, there's no such thing.

418
00:22:46,835 --> 00:22:49,045
Jane's just good at reading people,
among other things.

419
00:22:50,088 --> 00:22:51,131
How good?

420
00:22:52,007 --> 00:22:54,509
As good as you can be.
Got rich doing it.

421
00:22:57,554 --> 00:22:59,890
How does someone like that
end up working for the FBI?

422
00:23:01,683 --> 00:23:02,726
It's a long story.

423
00:23:03,602 --> 00:23:04,644
"We spotted her."

424
00:23:04,769 --> 00:23:06,563
"She's coming up the ramp. Alone."

425
00:23:07,481 --> 00:23:08,982
All right, let's move in.
You stay here.

426
00:23:16,364 --> 00:23:18,533
Tish DeLaurio!
Get on the ground right now!

427
00:23:18,658 --> 00:23:20,243
Don't move!
Stay where you are!

428
00:23:21,786 --> 00:23:23,705
Turn around
and get down on the ground.

429
00:23:23,997 --> 00:23:25,040
Don't shoot!

430
00:23:26,541 --> 00:23:27,667
I'm not armed.

431
00:23:31,880 --> 00:23:32,923
Stay back!

432
00:23:33,048 --> 00:23:34,090
- Don't hurt me.
- Stay back.

433
00:23:34,216 --> 00:23:35,425
- Please don't hurt me!
- Shut up.

434
00:23:35,550 --> 00:23:37,552
Please. Please don't hurt me!

435
00:23:57,864 --> 00:23:58,907
You okay?

436
00:23:59,199 --> 00:24:01,076
Sorry. You told me to stay.

437
00:24:01,952 --> 00:24:05,163
I did. Nice job.
Come on.

438
00:24:14,871 --> 00:24:16,539
"You have lost your mind, Abbott."

439
00:24:16,706 --> 00:24:18,708
Your people hounded my client

440
00:24:18,833 --> 00:24:20,585
abused her when they took her
into custody.

441
00:24:20,710 --> 00:24:22,253
Now you want her
to cooperate?

442
00:24:22,837 --> 00:24:24,130
There was no abuse, Ellen.

443
00:24:24,839 --> 00:24:27,759
- I got bruises.
- You ran, Tish.

444
00:24:28,509 --> 00:24:30,470
When people do that,
we chase after them.

445
00:24:30,595 --> 00:24:31,637
Of course she did.

446
00:24:31,763 --> 00:24:34,599
She was falsely accused of a crime
she has nothing to do with.

447
00:24:34,766 --> 00:24:36,517
Wait, wait.
You're not seriously suggesting

448
00:24:36,642 --> 00:24:38,853
- that she ran because, what? She's innocent?
- Ken.

449
00:24:40,897 --> 00:24:42,774
Now we believe
that your client is involved

450
00:24:42,899 --> 00:24:44,734
with the sale
of illegal weapons.

451
00:24:45,067 --> 00:24:46,360
It's a very serious crime.

452
00:24:47,361 --> 00:24:48,404
What's your evidence?

453
00:24:48,696 --> 00:24:50,907
The look on her face
when she was accused?

454
00:24:51,741 --> 00:24:54,160
We've been checking into
Tish's bank account.

455
00:24:54,786 --> 00:24:56,788
And there are
some substantial cash deposits.

456
00:24:57,538 --> 00:25:00,541
- I'm a bartender. I get tips.
- Oh, yeah.

457
00:25:01,042 --> 00:25:02,877
Some of which
were several thousand dollars.

458
00:25:03,753 --> 00:25:06,339
That's your argument?
She's a bad bartender?

459
00:25:07,340 --> 00:25:09,967
Look. We know
you didn't steal the guns

460
00:25:10,510 --> 00:25:12,094
you just work for the people
that did.

461
00:25:12,804 --> 00:25:13,971
Those are the people
that we want.

462
00:25:14,096 --> 00:25:17,266
So if you give us their names
this won't be so bad.

463
00:25:17,767 --> 00:25:18,851
Let her go right now

464
00:25:19,101 --> 00:25:20,520
or I'm going in front of a judge

465
00:25:20,645 --> 00:25:21,938
demanding her immediate release

466
00:25:22,063 --> 00:25:25,107
and filing charges for harassment
and false arrest.

467
00:25:26,192 --> 00:25:27,777
I guess we'll see you in court.

468
00:25:32,573 --> 00:25:33,616
Let's go.

469
00:25:43,209 --> 00:25:45,753
See this? This is exactly
what I was afraid of.

470
00:25:46,128 --> 00:25:48,965
So you be sure to tell Jane
I say thanks a lot.

471
00:25:57,723 --> 00:25:58,808
Think a judge will let her go?

472
00:25:59,392 --> 00:26:01,018
In a heartbeat.
We got nothing.

473
00:26:02,645 --> 00:26:03,688
We know where Jane is?

474
00:26:04,188 --> 00:26:05,356
Uh, about a half-hour ago

475
00:26:05,481 --> 00:26:07,483
he said he was going out
to read a report I got for him.

476
00:26:08,234 --> 00:26:10,486
- And Lisbon?
- Uh, she just left.

477
00:26:10,736 --> 00:26:11,863
Said she was going for a walk.

478
00:26:15,992 --> 00:26:17,118
Imagine that.

479
00:26:19,370 --> 00:26:22,748
Hey. I've been looking all over for you.
What are you doing out here?

480
00:26:22,915 --> 00:26:24,375
Oh, I just needed some air.

481
00:26:26,669 --> 00:26:27,712
What are you reading?

482
00:26:27,962 --> 00:26:30,464
FBI's psychological report
on Jeremy Geist.

483
00:26:30,590 --> 00:26:32,884
- Anything interesting?
- Couple things.

484
00:26:34,218 --> 00:26:36,888
- Any things to do with the case?
- Maybe.

485
00:26:37,889 --> 00:26:38,931
Jane.

486
00:26:40,266 --> 00:26:43,769
You don't need to wait until I need
to know to tell me things, okay?

487
00:26:44,186 --> 00:26:45,229
Not anymore.

488
00:26:48,691 --> 00:26:49,734
You're right.

489
00:26:50,443 --> 00:26:53,404
- Uh, it's okay...
- No. No. Please. Let me, uh...

490
00:26:54,697 --> 00:26:56,657
- Let me apologize. I'm sorry.
- It's fine.

491
00:26:57,575 --> 00:26:58,618
What's up?

492
00:26:59,118 --> 00:27:00,745
Well, I went
to Jeremy Geist's apartment

493
00:27:00,870 --> 00:27:03,497
and I noticed that he makes
his bed on the floor.

494
00:27:05,124 --> 00:27:07,376
And sleeps with a little
nightlight next to him.

495
00:27:07,668 --> 00:27:08,711
- Really?
- Mm.

496
00:27:09,545 --> 00:27:11,923
- Some kind of trauma?
- Childhood trauma, I'd imagine

497
00:27:12,048 --> 00:27:13,883
- so I, I checked it out.
- And?

498
00:27:14,592 --> 00:27:18,346
And feast your eyes on that.

499
00:27:20,348 --> 00:27:21,390
Whoa.

500
00:27:22,725 --> 00:27:26,687
16 years ago, there was a kidnapping
in Geist's hometown, Pittsburgh.

501
00:27:27,480 --> 00:27:29,440
A 12-year-old boy
named Justin Kellogg

502
00:27:29,565 --> 00:27:31,192
was taken by two kidnappers.

503
00:27:31,567 --> 00:27:32,985
They asked for $3 million
in ransom.

504
00:27:33,152 --> 00:27:35,488
The family paid it,
but they killed the boy anyway.

505
00:27:35,696 --> 00:27:37,573
They found his body
a couple weeks later.

506
00:27:37,907 --> 00:27:39,575
And what does that
have to do with Geist?

507
00:27:40,618 --> 00:27:41,911
Geist was a friend.

508
00:27:42,036 --> 00:27:44,372
He was staying over
the night Kellogg was taken.

509
00:27:51,462 --> 00:27:53,422
Shut up, kid! Or I'll have
your ass in a sling!

510
00:27:53,756 --> 00:27:55,341
"He told the police
he didn't see anything"

511
00:27:55,466 --> 00:27:56,759
"but he heard something."

512
00:27:59,261 --> 00:28:01,347
One of the kidnappers
cursed at Kellogg.

513
00:28:01,806 --> 00:28:03,849
Four months later,
a body turns up shot in the head

514
00:28:03,975 --> 00:28:05,393
with some of the ransom
money on it.

515
00:28:05,518 --> 00:28:07,687
That's one of the kidnappers.
His partner must have killed him.

516
00:28:08,187 --> 00:28:09,397
They ever get anything
on him? The partner?

517
00:28:09,563 --> 00:28:11,524
Never found or identified.

518
00:28:12,233 --> 00:28:14,860
The waitress said Geist was
spooked about something.

519
00:28:14,986 --> 00:28:17,071
You think Geist ran into the
missing kidnapper at the bar?

520
00:28:17,321 --> 00:28:18,906
Who then killed him, yes.

521
00:28:19,198 --> 00:28:20,992
- It's kind of a stretch.
- I know. I know.

522
00:28:21,117 --> 00:28:22,827
But I looked into
Geist's phone records.

523
00:28:23,035 --> 00:28:25,121
Yesterday, he called
the detective in Pittsburgh

524
00:28:25,246 --> 00:28:27,123
who investigated
the Kellogg kidnapping.

525
00:28:27,248 --> 00:28:28,290
Do you know what he said?

526
00:28:28,416 --> 00:28:30,167
Left a message,
said he wanted to talk to him.

527
00:28:31,043 --> 00:28:33,546
Okay. Yeah, I don't know. It's thin.

528
00:28:34,380 --> 00:28:35,923
And we have
a more pressing problem.

529
00:28:36,549 --> 00:28:40,052
- Oh, what's that?
- Tish DeLaurio is being released tomorrow.

530
00:28:40,678 --> 00:28:42,763
And we have to figure out a way
to keep her in custody

531
00:28:42,888 --> 00:28:45,558
otherwise, Spackman's case
is really dead

532
00:28:46,100 --> 00:28:47,143
and we killed it.

533
00:28:47,518 --> 00:28:48,686
Well, if she's selling guns

534
00:28:49,186 --> 00:28:50,563
she must have
a supply somewhere.

535
00:28:51,814 --> 00:28:52,940
We find that,
we can hold her.

536
00:28:53,524 --> 00:28:55,359
Well, we'd better do it
in the next 18 hours.

537
00:28:55,484 --> 00:28:57,445
How do we do that? She's not
gonna tell us anything.

538
00:28:57,778 --> 00:28:58,821
Exactly, Agent Vega

539
00:28:58,946 --> 00:29:01,866
which is how we're gonna crack
two cases for the price of one.

540
00:29:02,491 --> 00:29:03,576
I don't understand.

541
00:29:03,826 --> 00:29:05,911
You did a search for the gun
that killed Geist, right?

542
00:29:06,370 --> 00:29:08,622
Yeah. Searched a ten-block radius.
Didn't find a thing.

543
00:29:09,373 --> 00:29:11,625
- Perfect.
- Jane. Where have you been?

544
00:29:12,043 --> 00:29:13,502
- Getting this.
- A hammer?

545
00:29:13,836 --> 00:29:15,337
That's right.
That's a hammer.

546
00:29:15,546 --> 00:29:18,799
And with this, we are gonna nail
Tish and Geist's killer.

547
00:29:19,133 --> 00:29:22,094
Pardon the pun.
Oh, and someone's gonna have to stay up late.

548
00:29:22,803 --> 00:29:25,306
- How late?
- Very late.

549
00:30:17,956 --> 00:30:18,998
Morning, Tish.

550
00:30:19,708 --> 00:30:20,917
What is this?
What are you doing?

551
00:30:21,126 --> 00:30:23,044
We're gonna find those guns
you have hidden away.

552
00:30:24,212 --> 00:30:25,255
Don't know
how you're gonna do that.

553
00:30:25,880 --> 00:30:26,923
I'm not saying a word.

554
00:30:27,924 --> 00:30:29,884
That's what I'm relying on.
Let's go.

555
00:30:46,693 --> 00:30:48,945
Wylie, Vega,
you stay out here.

556
00:30:49,195 --> 00:30:51,072
Cho will give you the signal.
You have the hammer?

557
00:30:51,322 --> 00:30:53,032
Good. Radios?
All right.

558
00:30:57,078 --> 00:30:58,538
Why is Jane
telling everyone what to do?

559
00:30:58,788 --> 00:30:59,914
I thought Abbott was in charge.

560
00:31:00,165 --> 00:31:02,208
He is.
Except when Jane is.

561
00:31:02,751 --> 00:31:05,044
- And when is that?
- Uh, it, it kind of depends.

562
00:31:05,170 --> 00:31:07,464
Uh, it's okay. Abbott trusts him.
And Jane knows what he's doing.

563
00:31:09,591 --> 00:31:10,633
Usually.

564
00:31:12,469 --> 00:31:15,805
Excuse me. Ladies and gentlemen.
We're with the FBI.

565
00:31:17,056 --> 00:31:18,892
We're conducting a search
for some illegal

566
00:31:19,017 --> 00:31:21,436
and highly dangerous weapons
we believe are on the premises.

567
00:31:21,603 --> 00:31:24,314
And unless you work here,
I ask that you leave immediately.

568
00:31:24,481 --> 00:31:25,523
Thank you.

569
00:31:26,357 --> 00:31:28,568
Uh, sir, you can, uh, collect
your shoes later. Thank you.

570
00:31:29,527 --> 00:31:33,573
- What weapons?
- Uh, the ones Tish here's been selling.

571
00:31:34,783 --> 00:31:35,825
I need a witness.

572
00:31:36,326 --> 00:31:38,787
I'm here against my will,
without an attorney.

573
00:31:39,329 --> 00:31:40,538
It's a violation of my rights.

574
00:31:40,663 --> 00:31:42,791
Smile, agents,
you're on camera.

575
00:31:43,458 --> 00:31:44,501
What's going on?

576
00:31:44,626 --> 00:31:46,211
We believe Tish
is involved with a group

577
00:31:46,336 --> 00:31:47,629
that's selling illegal weapons

578
00:31:47,754 --> 00:31:49,005
and that
they're being stored here.

579
00:31:49,255 --> 00:31:51,633
- Here?
- Yes. And we're gonna find them.

580
00:31:51,758 --> 00:31:54,302
Little thing called the fourth amendment.
You need a warrant.

581
00:31:54,803 --> 00:31:57,347
- Don't you?
- Yes. And we can get one.

582
00:31:57,722 --> 00:31:59,682
But we'd have to shut you down
and tear the place up.

583
00:32:00,141 --> 00:32:01,810
But if you'll allow Mr. Jane
here to conduct a search

584
00:32:01,935 --> 00:32:03,937
- we can be done in 10 minutes.
- Five, even.

585
00:32:04,521 --> 00:32:05,563
Don't do it, Mason.

586
00:32:07,899 --> 00:32:09,484
Don't think
it should be a problem.

587
00:32:09,651 --> 00:32:10,693
All right. Thanks.

588
00:32:10,819 --> 00:32:12,028
Uh, uncuff her, please.

589
00:32:12,153 --> 00:32:14,239
We need her
to be able to move around.

590
00:32:14,697 --> 00:32:15,949
Whatever it is
you're looking for

591
00:32:16,783 --> 00:32:17,951
I don't know
anything about it.

592
00:32:18,076 --> 00:32:20,829
Then you have nothing to lose.
Take my hands.

593
00:32:22,163 --> 00:32:24,249
If you don't,
it's as good as confessing.

594
00:32:26,501 --> 00:32:28,336
- Whatever.
- Thank you.

595
00:32:29,420 --> 00:32:31,047
You think
you can keep a secret.

596
00:32:31,256 --> 00:32:33,883
But the harder you try,
the more you show.

597
00:32:34,425 --> 00:32:36,970
For example, Andy over there
doesn't want me to know

598
00:32:37,095 --> 00:32:39,639
about that foil wrapped
package of cocaine

599
00:32:39,764 --> 00:32:41,599
in his right-front pants pocket.

600
00:32:42,308 --> 00:32:43,351
That's crazy.

601
00:32:43,852 --> 00:32:45,353
Don't worry.
We're not narcs.

602
00:32:46,604 --> 00:32:48,606
You don't want me to know
where the guns are

603
00:32:48,898 --> 00:32:51,651
but you can't help react
when I get close.

604
00:32:52,443 --> 00:32:54,821
- I'm not.
- No, not over here.

605
00:32:55,530 --> 00:32:57,782
There's something going on
over here.

606
00:33:01,411 --> 00:33:03,079
We're not just dancing.

607
00:33:04,247 --> 00:33:05,790
Here, somewhere.

608
00:33:18,177 --> 00:33:19,429
What the hell is that?

609
00:33:22,140 --> 00:33:25,059
Military issue 45s. Looks like
there's about 20 of them.

610
00:33:26,561 --> 00:33:28,104
Oh, wait a damn minute.

611
00:33:28,229 --> 00:33:30,440
- Is that a rifle?
- Disassembled MK-4.

612
00:33:30,982 --> 00:33:32,025
"Voilà."

613
00:33:33,610 --> 00:33:34,819
Uh, no. You're a bunch of liars.

614
00:33:34,944 --> 00:33:37,530
I don't know what's going on
but I got nothing to do with this.

615
00:33:37,739 --> 00:33:39,574
Then how come you ran
when he called you out?

616
00:33:39,782 --> 00:33:41,784
- Excuse me? If...
- Hey, hey, hey.

617
00:33:41,910 --> 00:33:43,369
- Let go! Let go of me!
- No. I'm gonna take her outside.

618
00:33:43,494 --> 00:33:44,537
You finish here with Jane.

619
00:33:45,038 --> 00:33:46,623
- Let go!
- Okay, that was fun.

620
00:33:46,831 --> 00:33:48,249
- "Seriously! Let go!"
- Should we do a two-for-one?

621
00:33:48,583 --> 00:33:51,044
- What do you mean?
- We're gonna solve a second crime.

622
00:33:51,502 --> 00:33:53,004
Two connected crimes, actually.

623
00:33:53,212 --> 00:33:56,132
The kidnapping and murder
of a 12-year-old boy

624
00:33:56,507 --> 00:33:58,593
and the shooting of an FBI agent.

625
00:33:58,718 --> 00:34:00,678
The man that committed
those crimes is here.

626
00:34:01,429 --> 00:34:04,474
And the gun he used is too.
I'm gonna find both of them.

627
00:34:06,351 --> 00:34:08,478
- What was that?
- Nobody move. Just stay calm.

628
00:34:08,811 --> 00:34:11,189
"Lisbon! Tish got Vega's gun!
Keep everyone inside!"

629
00:34:11,314 --> 00:34:12,815
You heard him. Stay put.

630
00:34:16,486 --> 00:34:17,695
This is the cool part.

631
00:34:20,031 --> 00:34:21,741
Oh, my God.
She's trying to shoot at us.

632
00:34:21,866 --> 00:34:22,909
- We gotta get some cover.
- Kitchen! Come on!

633
00:34:23,034 --> 00:34:24,077
- Hey, come one.
- Get in the kitchen!

634
00:34:24,202 --> 00:34:25,244
- Go in the kitchen! Get in, quick!
- Kitchen.

635
00:34:25,370 --> 00:34:26,412
Go on, come on.

636
00:34:41,135 --> 00:34:43,388
Mr. Hunston, put down the gun.
Do it now.

637
00:34:49,602 --> 00:34:51,270
That's the gun that killed
Jeremy Geist, isn't it?

638
00:34:51,813 --> 00:34:54,065
The gun
and the man who used it.

639
00:34:54,649 --> 00:34:56,818
Did I call it
or did I call it?

640
00:35:01,072 --> 00:35:02,824
You kidnapped Justin Kellogg.

641
00:35:04,909 --> 00:35:07,203
And Jeremy Geist recognized you.
That's why you killed him.

642
00:35:08,162 --> 00:35:09,372
You know what they say
about karma.

643
00:35:10,039 --> 00:35:11,082
It's a bitch.

644
00:35:12,583 --> 00:35:16,087
Geist was a nobody to me.
Just another barfly.

645
00:35:18,172 --> 00:35:21,134
But the other night,
I said something to Tish.

646
00:35:21,592 --> 00:35:22,802
I was pissed, I guess.

647
00:35:24,012 --> 00:35:25,680
"Tish! Damn it!"

648
00:35:25,805 --> 00:35:28,182
I am sick and tired
of picking up slack for you!

649
00:35:28,349 --> 00:35:30,810
Now do it now, or I'll have
your ass in a sling!

650
00:35:37,942 --> 00:35:40,778
"I could tell it was something
I said. The way I said it."

651
00:35:41,279 --> 00:35:42,321
"He knew."

652
00:35:43,031 --> 00:35:45,366
He came up later,
asked me where I was from

653
00:35:45,867 --> 00:35:48,286
what I used to do.
Wasn't subtle.

654
00:35:49,203 --> 00:35:52,123
So when he came in the other night
I kept an eye on him.

655
00:35:55,835 --> 00:35:57,879
"Sure enough,
he broke into my office"

656
00:35:58,713 --> 00:36:00,089
"looking for evidence, I guess."

657
00:36:01,174 --> 00:36:02,425
Not that he was gonna find any.

658
00:36:04,427 --> 00:36:05,470
But that was it.

659
00:36:09,599 --> 00:36:11,017
I know you.

660
00:36:13,936 --> 00:36:15,605
Three million
is a lot of money.

661
00:36:16,355 --> 00:36:17,398
You killed
the other kidnapper

662
00:36:17,523 --> 00:36:19,108
so you could keep the ransom
for yourself, didn't you?

663
00:36:20,651 --> 00:36:22,820
Not saying I did,
not saying I didn't.

664
00:36:24,197 --> 00:36:25,490
But he didn't get it,
did he?

665
00:36:27,325 --> 00:36:31,287
Tish. I want to apologize to you
for earlier today.

666
00:36:31,412 --> 00:36:33,122
We didn't tell you
what was going on.

667
00:36:33,664 --> 00:36:35,083
Hope it wasn't
too uncomfortable.

668
00:36:35,875 --> 00:36:38,377
Don't worry.
It's all going into the lawsuit.

669
00:36:39,462 --> 00:36:41,380
Well, there's still
the matter of the guns.

670
00:36:42,590 --> 00:36:43,633
Don't waste your time.

671
00:36:44,342 --> 00:36:45,384
We know she won't talk.

672
00:36:45,510 --> 00:36:48,346
Uh, Tish, uh, what I did with you
earlier today was a fraud.

673
00:36:48,471 --> 00:36:51,766
We, in fact,
placed the guns in the bar.

674
00:36:52,350 --> 00:36:54,644
It's a trick that works,
and I'm gonna prove it to you.

675
00:36:54,769 --> 00:36:58,314
This is a map
of the neighborhood...

676
00:37:01,400 --> 00:37:02,443
around the bar.

677
00:37:03,111 --> 00:37:05,071
We know
you have the guns here.

678
00:37:05,404 --> 00:37:08,449
So, what I'm gonna do is
I'm gonna move my hands around

679
00:37:08,616 --> 00:37:11,202
and your reactions
are gonna show me where.

680
00:37:12,203 --> 00:37:14,622
- What the hell is this?
- See, this is the deal.

681
00:37:15,289 --> 00:37:18,000
If Tish agrees to cooperate
with Agent Spackman

682
00:37:18,251 --> 00:37:20,378
and tell him where
the location of the guns are

683
00:37:20,628 --> 00:37:23,422
and who she's been working with
she'll probably get a good deal.

684
00:37:24,674 --> 00:37:25,800
Minimal time.

685
00:37:26,217 --> 00:37:28,845
Definitely in here.

686
00:37:29,595 --> 00:37:31,764
But if she refuses to cooperate

687
00:37:31,973 --> 00:37:34,392
and Jane finds the guns
on this map here

688
00:37:35,101 --> 00:37:36,227
well, all bets are off.

689
00:37:37,019 --> 00:37:39,814
She gets the max.
25 to life.

690
00:37:41,190 --> 00:37:42,233
Here.

691
00:37:44,944 --> 00:37:46,112
Choice is yours.

692
00:37:49,699 --> 00:37:51,701
In here.

693
00:37:53,077 --> 00:37:54,120
This is absurd.

694
00:37:54,245 --> 00:37:55,997
- Come on, Tish. Let's go.
- Almost there.

695
00:37:59,333 --> 00:38:00,376
Tish!

696
00:38:04,797 --> 00:38:05,840
What do you want?

697
00:38:08,426 --> 00:38:09,468
Names?

698
00:38:10,261 --> 00:38:11,304
Yes.

699
00:38:12,054 --> 00:38:14,557
The people who have been stealing
the guns that you sell.

700
00:38:15,183 --> 00:38:18,019
Every one of them.
And the location of the guns.

701
00:38:18,519 --> 00:38:19,937
- Whatever you say...
- Sh.

702
00:38:27,528 --> 00:38:28,571
All right.

703
00:38:30,239 --> 00:38:31,282
You win.

704
00:38:32,533 --> 00:38:33,576
Good call.

705
00:38:34,410 --> 00:38:35,453
See?

706
00:38:36,162 --> 00:38:37,205
It's your birthday.

707
00:38:46,464 --> 00:38:48,132
Uh, excuse me.
Can I help you?

708
00:38:51,886 --> 00:38:52,929
Jane.

709
00:38:55,306 --> 00:38:56,349
Pike. Hello.

710
00:38:58,100 --> 00:39:00,269
I was, uh,
looking for Teresa.

711
00:39:01,896 --> 00:39:03,272
Yeah, I'm sure she's, um...

712
00:39:04,273 --> 00:39:05,524
I'm sure
she's around here someplace.

713
00:39:05,816 --> 00:39:06,901
Yeah, she probably is.

714
00:39:07,944 --> 00:39:08,986
Beard looks good.

715
00:39:10,029 --> 00:39:11,530
It's for an undercover thing.

716
00:39:15,326 --> 00:39:16,535
So, it's, uh...

717
00:39:18,663 --> 00:39:19,705
You and her.

718
00:39:21,916 --> 00:39:23,334
Yeah. Um...

719
00:39:27,880 --> 00:39:31,259
I'm sorry, we... we didn't intend
for it to happen like this.

720
00:39:33,469 --> 00:39:36,013
I know it was the last thing on her mind
the idea of hurting you.

721
00:39:37,556 --> 00:39:38,599
I know.

722
00:39:39,350 --> 00:39:40,393
I know that.

723
00:39:44,188 --> 00:39:45,439
So do you have a plan?

724
00:39:53,072 --> 00:39:54,699
Uh, I don't really understand.

725
00:39:55,283 --> 00:39:56,701
Well, I was offering her a life.

726
00:39:57,618 --> 00:40:00,621
A home, a family if she wanted it
a future.

727
00:40:02,248 --> 00:40:03,624
Have you thought
about any of that?

728
00:40:06,544 --> 00:40:08,170
I haven't thought
that far ahead yet.

729
00:40:09,547 --> 00:40:11,966
Well... Well, what are you offering her?

730
00:40:13,426 --> 00:40:15,386
I mean,
other than Patrick Jane?

731
00:40:20,308 --> 00:40:21,350
"Hey."

732
00:40:24,895 --> 00:40:26,105
Excuse me.

733
00:40:36,490 --> 00:40:37,533
What are you doing here?

734
00:40:38,159 --> 00:40:42,330
Well, I was upstairs,
giving a deposition and...

735
